une 1, 2026, so I need to figure out what messages came in between the last heartbeat and now. Let me convert the current timestamp to milliseconds—08:15 UTC converts to roughly 1779023700 in seconds, which gives me around 1,779,023,700,000 milliseconds.\n\nThe last heartbeat on the arbitration thread was at 1,778,975,602,235 milliseconds, so I'm looking for messages in the roughly 447,000 millisecond window between that time and now. Rather than calculating exact offsets, I should just fetch the latest messages and check what actually came through in that gap.\n","thinkingSignature":"a42bf3dbc4fd598608c0c0a412948a800bc153b36691da8c37336276401b97ac"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_i7t9zkis4gu1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check for newer messages - get the very latest messages\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=3&offset=0\" | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); msgs=d['messages']; print(f'Total messages: {d[\\\"total\\\"]}'); [print(f'ID:{m[\\\"id\\\"]} ts:{m[\\\"timestamp\\\"]} content:{m[\\\"content\\\"][:100]}') for m in msgs[:3]]\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2404,"output":751,"cacheRead":19398,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22553,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780301738744,"responseId":"066c72ab87fd53b1b2a9b65b2097b88d"}}
