{"type":"message","id":"ce3dbe20","parentId":"6e9273d7","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:16:56.955Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_mn5npxhmeocr_1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"messages\":[{\"id\":\"msg_1778975602235_skzwzl\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]**\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":1778975602235,\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1},\"replyTo\":null}],\"total\":773}"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":600,"aggregated":"{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"messages\":[{\"id\":\"msg_1778975602235_skzwzl\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]**\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":1778975602235,\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1},\"replyTo\":null}],\"total\":773}","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780301816951}}
{"type":"message","id":"c6983592","parentId":"ce3dbe20","timestamp":"2026-06-01T08:17:06.968Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so the API is working fine for GET requests with the X-API-Key header. But POST /send is returning error 1101. Let me try different approaches - maybe the endpoint path is different, or there's a different issue.\n\nActually, error 1101 with Cloudflare typically means \"Worker exceeded CPU time\" or \"Exceeded memory limits\". But that shouldn't be a consistent error for a simple POST.\n\nWait - looking at the issue, maybe the Cloudflare Worker is having trouble with the POST body or something. Let me try alternative approaches.\n\nActually, let me check if maybe the issue is that the current time is 08:15 UTC but the heartbeat messages show 23:50 UTC as the latest. There's a gap of about 8+ hours. Could this be from a previous session that ran before? The cron event is scheduled for 08:15 UTC, so maybe it hasn't been running through the night.\n\n\nThe POST /send endpoint is consistently returning error 1101, which is odd since GET requests work fine with the same authentication. Maybe there's something about how the request is being formatted or a rate limiting issue I'm hitting repeatedly.\n\nSince I'm running as part of a cron job, the messages are clearly being stored somehow—the heartbeat data from 23:50 UTC is already there from a previous execution. But if POST isn't working, I can't actually respond to the user's request right now. Let me see if I can extract any useful diagnostic information from the error itself, though the response body just shows the error code with no additional details.\n","thinkingSignature":"ebea8354022de1d82de3c0fa8775be80a48bcc92645fdee352a694ed1861d792"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_pluwsb4iqtmd_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with minimal content\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"OK\"}' 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":167,"output":416,"cacheRead":24422,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25005,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780301816956,"responseId":"066c72f99d49311bb3a3cbc581453dee"}}
